Yes—using Maxwell's Daemon replaces the entire mysqlbinlog | awk column-mapping script with a single, rock-solid open-source binary that outputs clean, real-column JSON events straight to /var/lib/db_sync/events.jsonl.
Maxwell handles binlog positions, column names, multi-line text, BLOB/JSON types, and schema changes automatically—while your POSIX file_to_peer.sh consumer reads events.jsonl line by line, turns each JSON event into an idempotent SQL statement (via jq), and streams it over WireGuard (10.99.0.x) with SET SESSION sql_log_bin = 0; so there are zero infinite sync loops.

